.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-or-later
.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt NQA2ID 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqa2id
.Nd Argon2id password hashing and key derivation
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqa2id
.Fa "const uint8_t *pw" "size_t pwlen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *salt" "size_t slen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *key" "size_t klen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ad" "size_t alen"
.Fa "uint32_t t" "uint32_t m" "uint32_t p"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t outlen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqa2id
computes Argon2id, version 0x13 (RFC 9106), of the password
.Fa pw
with
.Fa salt ,
the optional secret
.Fa key
and associated data
.Fa ad
.Dv ( NULL
with length 0 for none), making
.Fa t
passes over
.Fa m
KiB of memory in
.Fa p
lanes, and writes
.Fa outlen
bytes to
.Fa out .
.Pp
The limits, each refused with
.Dv NQEARG :
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Fa t
from 1 to
.Dv NQA2TMAX
(1024);
.It
.Fa p
from 1 to
.Dv NQA2PMAX
(255);
.It
.Fa m
from 8
.Fa p
to
.Dv NQA2MMAX
(4194304 KiB, 4 GiB); it is rounded down to a multiple of 4
.Fa p
blocks, as the RFC says, while the given value is what is hashed;
.It
a salt of at least
.Dv NQA2SMIN
(8) bytes, never
.Dv NULL ;
.It
an output of
.Dv NQA2OMIN
(4) to
.Dv NQA2OMAX
(1024) bytes;
.It
each input under 2^32 bytes.
.El
.Pp
In symbols (RFC 9106 sections 3.2 to 3.4), with H^n BLAKE2b with an
n-byte output, LE32 a 32-bit little-endian integer, q = 4 floor(m / 4p)
the columns of a lane, T =
.Fa outlen
and
.Sy ||
concatenation:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
H0 = H^64(LE32(p) || LE32(T) || LE32(m) || LE32(t) || LE32(0x13)
          || LE32(2) || LE32(|pw|) || pw || LE32(|salt|) || salt
          || LE32(|key|) || key || LE32(|ad|) || ad)
B[l][0] = H'^1024(H0 || LE32(0) || LE32(l))
B[l][1] = H'^1024(H0 || LE32(1) || LE32(l))
B[l][j] = G(B[l][j-1], B[l'][j'])           first pass
B[l][j] = B[l][j] ^ G(B[l][j-1], B[l'][j'])  later passes
C   = B[0][q-1] ^ ... ^ B[p-1][q-1]
out = H'^T(C)
.Ed
.Pp
where 2 is the type (Argon2id), G is the compression function of
section 3.5, (l', j') is chosen from the first 64-bit word of a
generated address block in slices 0 and 1 of the first pass and from
that of B[l][j-1] everywhere else, and H'^T(X) is H^T(LE32(T) || X) for
T at most 64, otherwise the first 32 bytes of each of
V1 = H^64(LE32(T) || X), V2 = H^64(V1), ..., Vr = H^64(Vr-1), with
r = ceil(T / 32) - 2, followed by H^(T-32r)(Vr).
.Pp
The memory is allocated once, through the allocator of
.Xr nqsetal 3 ,
and is wiped and freed before the call returns, on every path.
The lanes are filled one after another in the calling thread; the
result is the one the RFC's parallel order gives.
The second half of the first pass and all later passes read memory at
places that depend on the password, as Argon2id is designed to; a
process that shares a cache with an attacker can leak timing there.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK ,
or
.Bl -tag -width NQEMEM
.It Bq Er NQEARG
A parameter is outside the limits above, or a pointer is
.Dv NULL
with a nonzero length.
.It Bq Er NQELIM
.Fa m
KiB does not fit in a
.Vt size_t
(a 32-bit platform).
.It Bq Er NQEMEM
The allocation failed.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
uint8_t salt[16], k[32];
int rc = nqrand(salt, sizeof salt);
if (rc == NQOK)
  rc = nqa2id(pw, pwlen, salt, sizeof salt, NULL, 0, NULL, 0,
              3, 65536, 4, k, sizeof k);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqb2b 3 ,
.Xr nqpwenc 3 ,
.Xr nqsetal 3
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%A A. Biryukov
.%A D. Dinu
.%A D. Khovratovich
.%A S. Josefsson
.%T Argon2 Memory-Hard Function for Password Hashing and Proof-of-Work Applications
.%R RFC 9106
.%D September 2021
.Re
.Rs
